  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/235e19c4e3231eb22e6d43ccadcd90c5694077ec4ce562e6c4f188cfff77545f.png)\n\nIf the $3$ pancakes above are divided into ninths, then there will be{{field-1}}\nninths in total.",
  "worked_solution": "Since each part is $\\frac{1}{9}$ of a whole, we need to split each of the $3$ pancakes (wholes) into $9$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/6d7e91b7a982a8e5d4f17072484d0315663ae5c5187aefa49e8c756e785d530e.png)\n\n \n\nSo, we get $3\\times 9=27$ pieces in total.",
